From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: starfive: preserve active input on camera reselection

A V4L2 client may select its current input while probing or reopening the
camera. CAMSS unnecessarily reprogrammed that sensor, reset the ISP crop
and capture sizes, or returned EBUSY when PipeWire retained its buffers.

Resolve the selected link before testing queue ownership and return success
without changing the pipeline when it is already active. Real sensor
switches still reject either busy queue and retain rollback on failure.

The regression exercises the actual driver function: idle and busy
reselection must preserve a non-default crop and both capture formats.
It fails on the prior driver, which resets the crop even on reselection.
This fixes input selection semantics; it does not establish that either
sensor is electrically operational on the reported tablet.

Assisted-by: Codex (OpenAI)
---

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/starfive/camss/stf-video.c b/drivers/staging/media/starfive/camss/stf-video.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/starfive/camss/stf-video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/starfive/camss/stf-video.c
@@ -439,15 +439,6 @@
 	if (!stf_video_is_yuv(video))
 		return -EINVAL;
 	mutex_lock(&stfcamss->media_dev.graph_mutex);
-	ret = -EBUSY;
-	for (i = 0; i < STF_CAPTURE_NUM; i++) {
-		if (vb2_is_busy(&stfcamss->captures[i].video.vb2_q))
-			goto out;
-		saved_capture_formats[i] = stfcamss->captures[i].video.active_fmt;
-	}
-	if (media_entity_pipeline(&stfcamss->isp_dev.subdev.entity))
-		goto out;
-
 	ret = -ENOLINK;
 	mux = stf_video_find_subdev(video, MEDIA_ENT_F_VID_MUX);
 	if (!mux)
@@ -464,6 +455,24 @@
 			break;
 		}
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * V4L2 clients may reselect their current input after allocating buffers.
+	 * Keep its crop, formats and stream intact: no hardware change is needed.
+	 */
+	if (active_link == desired) {
+		ret = 0;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
+	ret = -EBUSY;
+	for (i = 0; i < STF_CAPTURE_NUM; i++) {
+		if (vb2_is_busy(&stfcamss->captures[i].video.vb2_q))
+			goto out;
+		saved_capture_formats[i] = stfcamss->captures[i].video.active_fmt;
+	}
+	if (media_entity_pipeline(&stfcamss->isp_dev.subdev.entity))
+		goto out;
 
 	ret = v4l2_subdev_call_state_active(&stfcamss->isp_dev.subdev,
 					    pad, get_selection, &saved_crop);
